         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/2ed24e37-3f1d-4d36-add5-664efd5b19dd,1793068380648/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C1920%2C1080%29%3B' alt='Photo of a man being interviewed' width='620' height='349' title='After the city&apos;s unofficial results were posted on Monday night, Tito-Dante Marimpietri spoke directly to Prime Minister Mark Carney during an interview with CBC&apos;s Christian D&apos;Avino, saying, &apos;you&apos;re going to get a phone call.&apos;'/><p>Tito-Dante Marimpietri will be the next mayor of Oshawa after cruising to a decisive win, according to the city's unofficial results page.</p>]]></description>
